  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to have a direct target relationship with Bone morphogenetic protein receptor type-1B through a chain of interactions involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence streams, each linking Oblonganoside C to a kinase (ICK, Fer) that is subsequently targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets the receptor. The consistent presence of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a mediator across all three paths suggests a central role in the signaling cascade. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of Ent-Gloeosteretriol's interaction with the receptor remains partially unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol in modulating the activity of the receptor, possibly through a kinase-dependent mechanism. The observed relationship underscores the importance of Ent-Gloeosteretriol in linking Oblonganoside C to the receptor, offering a plausible mechanism for the drug's biological effects.",
